.TH MULLION 1 "November 2026" "mullion 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mullion \- control inputs, screen layouts and KVM on DDC/CI monitors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mullion
.br
.B mullion
[\fB\-q\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B mullion \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments, opens the graphical application. With a command, performs
the action over DDC/CI using \fBddcutil\fR(1) and exits; this is what the
optional GNOME keyboard shortcuts, the Quick Settings menu and the screen-edge
switching run.
.PP
After an action, GNOME's on-screen pop-up shows what changed (or a
notification when the Mullion GNOME Shell extension isn't running).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the monitor, inputs, layout, brightness, contrast, volume and where the
keyboard and mouse are.
.TP
.B state
The same information as JSON, for the GNOME Quick Settings menu.
.TP
.B switch
With two inputs on screen, move the keyboard and mouse to the other
computer; otherwise switch the full-screen input between this and the other
computer.
.TP
.BR "usb " [ here | away | toggle ]
Move the monitor's USB hub (KVM) with the keyboard and mouse.
.TP
.BR "layout " [ list | next | \fINAME\fR]
List or select the screen layout:
.BR single ,
.BR 50-50 ,
.BR 75-25 ,
.BR 80-20 ,
.BR 25-75 ,
.BR 20-80 ,
.BR pip-small ,
.BR pip-large .
.B next
cycles through the layouts with two inputs.
.TP
.BR "pbp on" | off | toggle
Switch between the last used layout with two inputs and a single input.
.TP
.B swap
Swap the two inputs.
.TP
.BI "input " CODE
Select the main (left or full-screen) input by hex VCP code, e.g. 0x0f.
.TP
.BI "second " CODE
Select the second input (the right side or the inset).
.TP
.BR "brightness " [ \fIN\fR | +\fIN\fR | \-\fIN\fR]
.TQ
.BR "contrast " [ \fIN\fR | +\fIN\fR | \-\fIN\fR]
.TQ
.BR "volume " [ \fIN\fR | +\fIN\fR | \-\fIN\fR]
Show the value, set it (0\(en100) or change it relative to the current one.
.TP
.B inputs
List the inputs the monitor reports.
.TP
.B detect
Work out which input this computer is plugged into, from the connector
type, whether USB-C/Thunderbolt video is possible, the inputs on screen and
the current resolution.
.TP
.BR "cross " left | right
The pointer was pushed against this screen edge: if the other computer's
picture is on that side, move the keyboard and mouse to it. Run by the GNOME
Shell extension.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Don't show what changed on screen.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mullion/config.json
Settings that differ from the defaults: input roles and names, enabled
features, and VCP codes overriding those of the U4025QW for other models.
.SH NOTES
The user needs read/write access to the monitor's /dev/i2c-* device. The
ddcutil package grants this to the user logged in at the local desktop;
otherwise add the user to the \fBi2c\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcutil (1)
